From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:54:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system/cpus: run_on_cpu under record/replay: release the
 replay mutex while waiting

Under record/replay the main loop holds the replay mutex with the BQL. A vCPU thread that has
started running takes the replay mutex before serving queued work, so synchronous work requested
from the main loop (x86 vapic_post_load on a loadvm after start) deadlocks. Let the vCPU have the
mutex while we wait and re-take both in lock order.

NEEDS REVIEW: dropping and retaking the BQL inside run_on_cpu changes its locking contract for
every caller under replay. From observe's rr spike (gate/rrux).
---
 system/cpus.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/cpus.c b/system/cpus.c
index 97e5a5edee23b70d8bd170c2b984568f4e804672..f7f83899d0d6992458f8a725b0515c5ec5c9c8f1 100644
--- a/system/cpus.c
+++ b/system/cpus.c
@@ -438,6 +438,23 @@ void qemu_init_cpu_loop(void)
 
 void run_on_cpu(CPUState *cpu, run_on_cpu_func func, run_on_cpu_data data)
 {
+    /*
+     * rrux: under record/replay the main loop holds the replay mutex while
+     * it holds the BQL.  A vCPU thread that has started running takes the
+     * replay mutex before it serves queued work (tcg-accel-ops-rr.c), so
+     * synchronous work requested from the main loop (x86 vapic_post_load on
+     * a loadvm after start, e.g. x-rr-begin-record) deadlocks.  Let the
+     * vCPU have the mutex while we wait; re-take it in lock order.
+     */
+    if (replay_mode != REPLAY_MODE_NONE && !current_cpu &&
+        replay_mutex_locked() && bql_locked()) {
+        replay_mutex_unlock();
+        do_run_on_cpu(cpu, func, data, &bql);
+        bql_unlock();
+        replay_mutex_lock();
+        bql_lock();
+        return;
+    }
     do_run_on_cpu(cpu, func, data, &bql);
 }
 
